      "reason": "All five arrays are declared immediately before their guard and before being filled. Value initialization/reference binding do not throw normally; all arrays outlive their guard and never move or escape. No owning callable allocation is needed to establish cleanup."
    },
    {
      "claim_challenged": "Original ordinary return/false/cancel paths not broken",
      "conclusion": "SUSTAINED_SOURCE_ONLY",
      "evidence": [
        "SW6",
        "SW7",
        "SW8"
      ],
      "id": "C3",
      "reason": "Original explicit wipes remain, so earliest normal cleanup timing and bool/status decisions do not move. Repeated zero stores at scope exit are safe. Early pre-copy cancellation holds no target local secret; late false/cancel paths retain guards. No new synchronization or cancellation/publication branch."
    },
    {
      "claim_challenged": "C++ exception cleanup after realistic allocation cuts",
      "conclusion": "SUSTAINED_CONDITIONAL_SOURCE_ONLY",
      "evidence": [
        "SW1",
        "SW2",
        "SW3",
        "SW6",
        "SW7",
        "SW8"
