      "id": "C4",
      "reason": "AAD reserve sees guarded populated PRF and zero wrapping array; second-HMAC allocation sees guarded PRK plus outer PRF and zero output key; AES/later enrollment allocation sees guarded wrapping+PRF. Export catches occur only after acquisition stack unwinds. Actual production failure reachability and residue remain unexecuted."
    },
    {
      "claim_challenged": "Caller key/output ownership and compatibility",
      "conclusion": "SUSTAINED_SOURCE_ONLY",
      "evidence": [
        "SW1",
        "SW6",
        "SW7",
        "SW8",
        "ST2"
      ],
      "id": "C5",
      "reason": "KDF guards its own PRK, never caller output. Enrollment never borrows const vault_key; retrieval never guards out_vault_key. Committed decrypted output survives. Valid-shape raw retrieval prezero/non-OK/catch wipes and localized validation prezero are unchanged. No ABI/format/KDF/AAD/credential identity/dependency/version/signing/release change; existing roundtrip source is not a known-answer result."
    },
    {
      "claim_challenged": "Synthetic tests measure cleanup and isolate dispatch honestly",
